<title>FINLAND: STARCKJOHANN SEES LOWER 1996 EARNINGS.</title>
<headline>STARCKJOHANN SEES LOWER 1996 EARNINGS.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1996-10-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finnish hardware wholesaler and retailer Starckjohann Oy said in a statement on Thursday it expected full-year 1996 earnings to be somewhat lower than in 1995 despite a better performance in September-December.</p>
<p>&quot;The group's earnings for the final tertial are expected to be better than last year, but due to the weak beginning of the year, earnings for the financial year are expected to remain somewhat below last year's,&quot; Starckjohann said in its January-August interim report.  </p>
<p>In 1995, Starckjohann's profit after financial items was 78.7 million markka. In January-August, the group's profit fell almost 22 percent to 57.4 million markka.</p>
<p>--Helsinki Newsroom  +358 - 9 - 680 50 245</p>
